  "description": "MOBILE, Ala. - U.S. Coast Guard Aviation Training Center Mobile, Ala., deploys an MH-60 Jayhawk rescue helicopter and crew to Coast Guard Air Station New Orleans as part of the Coast Guard's pre-staging efforts in response to Tropical Storm Ida, Nov. 9, 2009.  The Coast Guard stages assets in safe locations as hurricanes or tropical storms pass and then re-deploy them into affected areas to perform search and rescue operations. \n\nU.S. Coast Guard video by Petty Officer 2nd Class Thomas M. Blue",
